<h2 id="features">Features, placement and variants</h2>

The pinned frontend registers 53 feature types, and the [interface coverage inventory](../reference/ha-interface-coverage.json) maps each one to its guidance. Show only the features and options the native card and entity support. Tile feature placement is bottom or inline. When you move a feature, keep its label and reading order. A configured mode list must not add modes the device lacks.

| Feature family | Native variants to keep | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Climate, fan, humidifier and water-heater mode choices | Dropdown or icons, where that feature offers them | Give every icon a text equivalent. Use a dropdown when labels need room. |
| Select options | Dropdown or buttons | Show the native option labels and keep the stored value. |
| Numeric input, target temperature and target humidity | Buttons or slider | Keep bounds, steps and units. Offer exact entry where the native flow supports it. |
| Timer presets | Buttons or dropdown | A duration choice is not an elapsed-time reading. |
| Cover and valve favourites; light colour favourites | Named or value-based shortcuts | A favourite is a requested setting. It does not confirm the current position or colour. |
| Bar gauge, trend and forecast | Read-only displays | Show the quantity, period and a text value. Never present a gauge as an adjustable slider. |

Do not turn every feature into a filled icon tile. Use one consistent Material Design Icons (MDI) set for domain actions, 24px icons where suitable, square surfaces, quiet dividers and the shared spacing scale. Keep a domain colour only when its meaning is also explained without colour.

