<h2 id="badges">Badges, headings, headers and footers</h2>

Entity and state-label badges summarise one identified state. Power, gas and water total badges need units and the selected period. An alert badge needs the real alert meaning. A shortcut badge must name its destination. An entity-filter badge has the same empty-or-failed distinction as a filtered card. An error badge shows a failure, so do not use it as a general warning icon.

Heading badges can show entity values or buttons. Give them accessible names that make sense outside the heading. A picture header gives context. A graph header or footer needs a matching summary. A button header or footer must hold real actions. Do not add a decorative chart strip without a quantity and period. Not every card or view accepts every badge, header or footer, so keep the native differences.

