<h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance checks</h2>

Check all four native layouts with long names, 320px width, keyboard order and enlarged text. Change a feature’s capabilities while details are open. No unsupported command may stay active. Try empty filters, unknown states, a hidden view opened by URL and partial groups. A display filter must not act as a permission check. Check native dropdown and icon variants separately, and make sure the selection is announced in text.

Sources: [Views](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/views/), [Card features](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/features/), [Badges](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/badges/), [Card headers and footers](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/header-footer/) and the [pinned feature registry](https://github.com/home-assistant/frontend/blob/e32bc0696ebefde323f5b791269ad0c57f3f99d9/src/panels/lovelace/card-features/registry.ts).

<h2 id="evidence">Implementation and evidence boundary</h2>

This page is a design reference. It does not replace native Home Assistant components. Mapping a registry entry here gives it a design owner. It does not show that every integration, browser or device has been tested. Keep native state formatting, translations, permissions, capabilities and event handling. Theme tokens change presentation. They cannot supply behaviour the application lacks.

Record what was tested using [Native task accessibility and evidence](native-task-accessibility.html). Recheck native behaviour after a frontend change.

Keep native 16px control text, visible labels, keyboard access and readable names at 320px. A compact arrangement must not remove an explanation of what a control can do or a way to recover. Use the quiet border token for structural dividers, and keep editable boundaries and focus indicators distinct. See [Structure](../styles/structure.html) and the shared [design styles](../styles/index.html).

Source baseline: Home Assistant Core 2026.11.1 and frontend 20261028.5. Primary documentation reviewed on 12 November 2026.
